0 405 385 [
[(This is a classic rotating-tape-head style pitch)]
[(shifter using the [delread4~] variable delay)]
[(object. There are two moving tape heads, each of)]
[(which is loudest at the middle of its trajectory,)]
[(and enveloped out at the moment it has to jump)]
[(back \050or forward\051 to start another scratch. Most)]
[(of the brain work is in computing how fast the)]
[(tape heads have to move to get the desired)]
[(transposition.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 405 142 [
[(The [cos~] objects compute the fadein and fadeout)]
[(of the two delay line outputs. They each traverse)]
[(the positive half of the cosine waveform \050phase)]
[(-0.25 to +0.25\051 over the time the phase goes from)]
[(one end to the other.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 405 243 [
[(The "window size" is the total trajectory of the)]
[(read points in the delay line, in milliseconds.)]
[(The delay times are controlled by a [phasor~])]
[(object. The second delay time, 180 degrees out of)]
[(phase from the first one, is computed using the)]
[([wrap~] object.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
